BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:state-pte-alaska-2025-04-15@ustaxcalendar.com
DTSTAMP:20260924T122623Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20250415
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20250416
SUMMARY:Alaska: Form 6900 due
DESCRIPTION:Alaska requires a partnership (or LLC taxed as a partnership) w
 ith nexus in Alaska to file Form 6900 only if at least one partner/member i
 s a corporation or another partnership (a partnership whose partners are al
 l natural persons is not required to file). The Alaska partnership return i
 s due 30 days after the federal partnership return's due date (not the same
  calendar date each year\, since it tracks the federal due date including a
 ny weekend/holiday shift) - for the 2025 tax year\, 30 days after the feder
 al 1065 due date of March 16\, 2026\, is April 15\, 2026. Separately\, an S
  corporation doing business in Alaska must file Form 6000 (the same corpora
 te income tax return C corporations use)\, but Alaska does not tax the S co
 rporation on its pass-through income\; most S corporations satisfy the fili
 ng obligation by completing only page 1 and checking the S Corporation box\
 , unless the corporate-level built-in-gains or excess-net-passive-income ta
 x applies. | Alaska Form 6900 (Partnership Information Return) is due 30 da
 ys after the federal partnership return's due date - April 15\, 2026 for th
 e 2025 tax year (30 days after the federal 1065 due date of March 16\, 2026
 ) - and is required only when at least one partner is a corporation or anot
 her partnership\; a partnership with only natural-person partners has no Al
 aska filing requirement. A federal extension automatically extends the Alas
 ka due date to 30 days after the federal extended due date (October 15\, 20
 26). S corporations doing business in Alaska separately file Form 6000 (the
  corporate return)\, though Alaska generally does not tax S corporations on
  pass-through income. | Authority: Alaska Department of Revenue\, Instructi
 ons for Form 6900 (Alaska Partnership Information Return): "A partnership o
 r an LLC treated as a partnership for tax purposes ... which conducts busin
 ess in the state (also known as having 'nexus' with the state) is required 
 to file Form 6900. If all of the partners or LLC members ... are natural pe
 rsons or are effectively treated as natural persons\, the partnership is no
 t required to file Form 6900." "The Alaska partnership return must be filed
  within 30 days of the date on which the partnership's federal return is re
 quired to be filed." "A federal extension automatically extends the Alaska 
 filing due date to 30 days after the federal extended due date." S-corp tre
 atment per Instructions for Form 6000: "An S Corporation doing business in 
 Alaska is required to file an Alaska return\, but Alaska does not impose a 
 tax on the S Corporation for pass-through items of income\," subject to the
  built-in-gains and excess-net-passive-income exceptions. Direct access to 
 tax.alaska.gov is blocked by robots.txt for automated fetch (confirmed agai
 n this session)\; the quoted language above is from the Department's own Fo
 rm 6900i and 6000i instruction PDFs\, accessed via two independently-hosted
  verbatim mirrors of the same official documents (identical wording on both
 )\, rather than a direct tax.alaska.gov fetch. | Source: https://www.taxfor
 mfinder.org/forms/2024/2024-alaska-form-6900i.pdf | This date is computed f
 rom a recurrence rule and may not reflect a later-announced change\; confir
 m against the cited source before relying on it.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
