 er the federal extended due date (October 15\, 2026). S corporations doing 
 business in Alaska separately file Form 6000 (the corporate return)\, thoug
 h Alaska generally does not tax S corporations on pass-through income. | Au
 thority: Alaska Department of Revenue\, Instructions for Form 6900 (Alaska 
 Partnership Information Return): "A partnership or an LLC treated as a part
 nership for tax purposes ... which conducts business in the state (also kno
